This is important. The graph build:
- `entities.append({"entity_name": title, ..., "source_id": entity_source_id, "file_path": file_path})`

Each page appends an entity with entity_name=title. If two pages have the SAME title, they produce two entities with the SAME entity_name but DIFFERENT source_id (chunk:title:0) and DIFFERENT file_path. But the source_id is also `chunk:{title}:0` — SAME for both! So both entities have source_id `chunk:X:0`, and the chunks also have `chunk:X:0`, `chunk:X:1`, etc. for BOTH pages (same chunk IDs!).

So actually, the title collision is DEEPER than just path_map:
1. `path_map` (in graph_state.json) keyed by title → collision.
2. entities: two entities with same entity_name, same source_id → LightRAG might dedupe or overwrite.
3. chunks: both pages produce `chunk:X:0`, `chunk:X:1` → same chunk IDs → collision in chunk_to_source_map.

